WEBVTT

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.280
<i>Joe!</i>

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.280
<i>Joe!</i>

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.870
<i>I think I understand what you're saying, Joe.</i>

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:40.910
<i>But do you have to cling to boxing and degrade yourself as a touring boxer?</i>

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.290
<i>Come on! Why don't you work at Hayashi's with me?</i>

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:44.750
<i>Don't go, Joe!</i>

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.920
<i>You can't just up and leave now!</i>

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.590
<i>You can't! Right, Joe!?</i>

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.470
Cling to the ring and degrade myself to a touring boxer?

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.890
It's not that big a deal.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:01.680
I'm just going on a little trip.

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:06.640
That's all.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.770
Hey, Sachi! Where are we going?

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.990
Over by the field!

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.830
Hey, keep it down, you little brats!

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:22.950
People are trying to sleep here!

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.790
Hey, why the hell are the kids so noisy these days?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:30.340
They've been making a fuss about buying Joe a farewell gift before he leaves.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:33.510
Hey, is it true that Joe's leaving?

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.220
What, you haven't heard?

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.550
Apparently he's going touring, cause he can't box here in Tokyo.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:39.470
Really?

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.760
Oh, I didn't know!

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.850
Leaving, huh...

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.140
Sure is gonna be lonely around here without Joe.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:49.610
Hey, Missus... I think it'd be nice to give Joe a farewell gift of our own.

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.600
What do you think?

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.700
Let's see... That makes 152 yen.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.910
No way! It's 155 yen!

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.490
There's three yen right here, don't you see?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.950
I counted that already.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.160
Either way, we can't get him anything.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.630
We tried so hard, and we've got nothing to show for it...

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:10.590
Don't get so down about it, Sachi.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:14.210
It's not about the money. It's the thought that counts.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.710
That's it! I've got a good idea!

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:24.300
What's going on?

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.480
Cut this out at once!

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.350
Shut up! Now, you gonna sell it or not?

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.530
H-Hey! What the blazes is going on here?

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:36.570
Oh, High Priest!

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.820
These children want to buy a talisman for only 150 yen, and won't stop asking about it!

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.000
What do you mean, "only"?

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.910
Yeah! My Joe's going on a journey!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.290
And we brought all the money we could get our hands on!

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:47.790
Oh, going on a journey, is he?

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.410
We can't sell you one, in that case.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:51.910
Oh, really? Then how about this?

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.630
H-Hey! Stop this at once!

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.130
Ow...

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:05.010
Fools! We only have talismans for childbirth!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.430
Childbirth?

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:28.490
Joe!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.080
Why are you in such a panic?

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.210
N-Noriko! Joe's...

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.580
Joe's gone!

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.920
I just noticed when I woke up.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.590
It looks like Joe got up and left while I was sleeping!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.680
I thought he was leaving this evening!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.010
You're right!

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.310
O-Old man!

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.060
Old man! Wake up!

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.850
Old man! Old man!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.570
Old man! Joe's gone!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.160
Old man! Come on, old man!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.740
It's no good. He's so drunk he can't hear a word I say.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.370
Noriko, let's go over to the station and see if he's there!

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:11.830
Sure.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.790
We might still make it. Come on!

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.850
Danpei-san must've known that Yabuki-kun was leaving this morning.

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:34.810
Y-You think so?

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.770
Yes. I'm sure.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.360
Danpei-san was so sad he couldn't say a thing.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.460
Old man!

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.500
Morning, old man! Where's Joe?

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.460
We brought him a parting gift!

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:04.390
Joe!

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.390
<i>Bro Joe!</i>

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.220
Morning, Joe!

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:05.960
Morning!

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.550
<i>Come on, Joe!</i>

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.470
Joe's already gone.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.510
What did you say?

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:15.060
Nishi and Noriko-san just went to the station.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:16.480
You kids should go, too.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.560
Joe...

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.930
Joe!

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.980
Wh-What about you, old man?

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:26.740
Me?

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.080
I've already said my goodbyes.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:02.230
A trip, huh... It's been a while since I last went on the road.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.360
Hey, mister!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.200
What?

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.370
Do you like trains, too?

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:12.910
Yeah, they're nice.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.700
Are you gonna ride a train?

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.750
Yeah, I sure am.

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:17.580
Where are you going?

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.870
I still don't know.

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:26.130
But you're lucky! I wish I could ride a train, too!

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.130
<i>Why?</i>

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.380
Why? I just wanna go somewhere far away.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.390
Somewhere far away...

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.640
You're going to the station, aren't you?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:36.600
Yeah.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.440
Then let's go together!

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:39.850
What? You wanna go, too?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.360
I go there once every day!

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.900
I'm saving up money to go somewhere far away someday,

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.820
but until then, I'm happy to just play at the station!

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:49.490
I see.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.950
Then let's go to the station together!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:52.700
Sure!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.500
I actually like steam trains more.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.130
Electric trains are fine, but steam trains are better.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.760
A steam train would be better for going far away.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.550
We're here, bro!

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.710
Sure is fun being at the station!

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:26.400
You think so?

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.400
Yeah, there are so many different people, all in the same place!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.240
Yeah, you got a point.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.530
There are country folk and Tokyo folk, students, old people, and kids...

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.280
There are even pickpockets!

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.280
And look who's here today!

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:40.540
Who's that?

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:41.670
A detective!

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:43.880
A detective?

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.960
Yeah. He specializes in runaway kids.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.550
He mistook me twice for a runaway, so he remembers me.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:58.520
I think he said he'd be at the station by 4:30 p.m...{write it out unless pm is used}

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.520
Maybe he's not here because it's not even three yet?

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.150
Let's just look for him anyway.

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:15.740
I've actually decided where I want to go.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.030
Oh?

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.620
Where do you think? You wanna guess?

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.120
I wonder...

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:21.620
Tohoku?

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:22.830
Wrong!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:24.580
Then how about Osaka?

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.420
No way!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:26.540
Oh, I know! Kyushu!

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.370
Wrong again!

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.090
It's not overseas, is it?

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:33.720
You're kidding! How can I go overseas on a train?

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.390
It's a secret!

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:37.840
If you get it right, then congrats!

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.390
Maybe Yabuki-kun's already gone.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.350
No, he shouldn't be.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:46.610
Let's look a little harder.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.350
Come on. Let's go.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.320
What time's your train?

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.740
I don't know. Someone's supposed to go with me.{Stupid Keyframe lol}

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.530
When's he coming?

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.500
Well, there's still time.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:03.080
I'm hungry, though. Wanna eat something?

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:03.960
Would ramen be fine?

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.420
I know a good place!

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:06.330
Let's go!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:07.050
Sure.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.800
This way! Come on!

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.920
Right here! It's really good!

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:18.310
Hey!

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.850
Watch yourself, kid!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.270
You watch yourselves, idiots!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.520
What was that?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:32.190
Let me go!

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:34.020
What do you think you're doing, you brat?

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.020
<i>Let me go!</i>

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:35.240
Let me go!

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.990
You little bastard!

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:36.990
<i>That hurts, stupid!</i>

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:37.690
Quit it.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:44.240
That's no way to treat a child.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:48.750
Is that brat there your lackey?

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:52.290
Come on, kid. Let's go eat.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:53.380
Hold it.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:54.420
Hey, kid!

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.550
I said hold it! Are you deaf?

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.300
Hey!

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.300
You wanna fight, punk?

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.560
You're not actually serious about this, are you?

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:15.570
And what if I am?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:17.070
Mister...

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:50.730
Don't do it!

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:54.650
Ina-chan!

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:57.650
Don't start a fight. Not here.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.820
But bro, this son of a-{dunno whether to joint or overlap, there's small overlapping}{Boss?}

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.830
<i>I said don't, you idiot!</i>

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:03.610
All right.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.120
Sorry about that. Let him off the hook, okay?

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.170
It's fine.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.670
Don't make a fool of yourselves.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:20.930
He may be a touring boxer, but he's still a boxer.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:21.930
You don't wanna get in a fight with him.

00:12:21.930 --> 00:12:24.630
S-Sorry about that. I just got pissed, and...

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:29.100
And he was just such a creepy son of a bitch that we got ready to throw down.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.770
Didn't you have any idea who he was?

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.360
Who?

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:36.980
No idea...

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.990
Yeah, who was he?

00:12:38.990 --> 00:12:43.030
I bet you didn't. You wouldn't have caused this ruckus if you had.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:46.080
That guy's one of us. The star of our troupe.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.040
You mean he's...

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:52.250
He's Yabuki Joe, the guy who killed Rikiishi?

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:58.170
What do you think, mister? Isn't it good?

00:12:58.170 --> 00:12:59.750
Yeah, it's good.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.010
That was a real close shave, sir!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.930
You gotta be careful! Tokyo's full of dangerous types!

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:11.060
Well, even I had a little run-in with them when I first got here...

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.980
Mister! This guy's just about to leave!

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:19.690
Oh, my apologies!

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.860
Going on a journey, are you?

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:26.530
You see, this kid never stops talking about going on a journey.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:29.660
Well? When do you think you're gonna go?

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:31.870
To Hokkaido, like you're always talking about.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:34.870
Oh, I see. Hokkaido.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.210
Hey, that was a secret!

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:42.260
Oh my! I'm sorry about that.

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:55.430
Did you go that way, Nishi-kun?

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:58.940
No, let's keep going this way.

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:11.450
Hey, what kept you?

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:14.460
Yeah, sorry about that.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.660
Did you wait long?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.340
Yeah, I guess. Time is money, after all.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:21.670
Let's see... That only leaves Yabuki.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:25.800
Our star's having dinner right now.{dinner at 4:30?}

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.680
That was delicious! Thanks for the food!

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:35.560
No, this is my food! I'll pay for it myself!

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.270
It's all right. I'll cover it.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:38.900
No, it's not all right!

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:40.690
Come on. Don't be shy.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.740
No, that's not it!

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:45.150
Aren't you about to go on a trip?

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.910
You've gotta save your money!

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.450
You shouldn't be wasting it here!

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:51.580
Yeah.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.330
You're right.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.250
Let's go Dutch, then.{or "let's split it"}

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:55.990
Okay?

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:58.040
Thanks for your business!

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:03.130
I'm gonna save up as much as I can to go to Hokkaido!

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:06.000
What do you think Hokkaido's like?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.260
Let's see... I don't have a clear image...

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.510
But it's wide, has good scenery, and it's cold, right?

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.930
Okay! Then I'll show you!

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.010
This way!

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.100
H-Hey!

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:21.110
H-Hey! Don't pull me like that!

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:22.150
What are you gonna show me?

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:23.490
Hokkaido!

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:50.680
I see. Hokkaido's a pretty place.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:54.890
Isn't it great?

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:55.720
Don't you wanna go?

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.690
Sometimes they change the pictures,

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:00.730
so I always look forward to that.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.770
Hey, isn't that a steam engine?

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.990
Isn't it cool?

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.030
A steam engine looks good in the snow.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:11.530
Oh, yeah! Ever wanted to go to Abashiri?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.740
Abashiri?

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:17.040
Remember? Like from the song "Abashiri Prison"!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:27.340
Far... Far away is the Okhotsk...

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:34.010
The crimson red roses...

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:35.510
Oh, no!

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.510
My mom's gonna be home soon!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.560
I have to go home and help with her side job!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.610
I see. That must be hard.

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:46.520
No, when I think of doing it to go to Hokkaido, it's really okay.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:48.030
Keep it up.

00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:50.650
Save up a lot of money, and go to Hokkaido someday.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.030
Oh, I sure will!

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:54.990
Well, you take care now!

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:55.780
Yeah.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:56.790
Goodbye!

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:57.660
Goodbye.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.120
Mister!

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:06.460
Guys like you are really cool!{"I really like guys like you" makes him sound a bit gay}

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:07.760
Goodbye!

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:19.930
Hear me now, sister...

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:24.810
Do not fall in love with a mountain man!

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:31.150
'Cause if he gets caught in a mountain wind, you'll become a young widow...

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.440
Joe!

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:35.150
I've been waiting for you, Yabuki!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.240
Hey.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.240
Don't bother with the greetings.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.740
Now, I heard you met these guys a little while ago.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:43.920
Yeah, sorry about earlier.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:46.750
I had no idea you were the famous Yabuki Joe.{infamous? tlc}

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.840
Well, we've got a lot of reckless folks in this business.

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.800
But I hope you can get along with them anyway.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.170
Yeah. There was another one I met earlier.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.680
The name's Inaba. Nice to meet you.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:00.980
Inaba-san, huh?

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:03.230
I could swear I've heard that name before.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:07.640
Forget it. The past means nothing to us now.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:10.150
Well, it's time to go! Let's get moving!

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:15.320
I'm worn out! My ass hurts!

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:20.950
These burdens really make it hard on us ham actors.

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:22.370
No kidding!

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:29.630
<i>Ina No. 8 Express to Akita boarding at platform 14!</i>

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:34.170
<i>Hakutaka No. 3 Limited Express to Kanazawa boarding at platform 15!</i>

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:40.720
<i>Yuzuru No. 4 Express to Aomori via the Joban Line boarding at platform 16!</i>

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.850
Hey! This way!

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:38.170
Yeah.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.180
Guess this is goodbye to Tokyo.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.640
That was easier than I thought.

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:02.280
Joe!

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.120
Looks like they're here to see you off, Yabuki.

00:19:05.750 --> 00:19:08.710
I'll save your seat. Say your goodbyes all you want.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:11.920
Joe!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:13.920
You've been looking for me?

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.390
Idiot! Why did you leave without saying anything?

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:20.510
We were worried sick about you!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.140
Why can't you think about how Noriko and I feel?

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.430
A-At least a little...

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:27.730
Oh, come on, Nishi! I thought you were a man!

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:29.730
You're so emotional.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:33.400
It's not like I'm leaving for good, you know.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.610
So, where's the old man?

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:39.940
The old man got drunk...

00:19:41.330 --> 00:19:42.530
I see.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.080
The old man's drunk, huh?

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.450
It was hard for him to say goodbye to you.

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:50.920
Well, that's out of character.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:55.960
<i>The train at platform 16 will leave at 5:50 p.m.!</i>

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:59.470
<i>Bound for Aomori, via the Joban Line!</i>

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:02.340
<i>All riders heading to Aomori...</i>

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.350
Well, that's quite enough.

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:03.430
I'll be back.

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.850
Joe, can't you stay a little longer?

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:05.890
Yabuki-kun!

00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.060
Here.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.480
Eat this later.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.690
I see.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.270
Well, guess I'll take it.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:15.570
That'll save me some money.

00:20:15.570 --> 00:20:16.980
Joe!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:18.480
Bro!

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:18.480
<i>Joe!</i>

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.990
Joe! Joe!

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:22.990
Bro!

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:23.910
Joe!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:28.910
You dummy! Why'd you leave without saying anything, you big dummy?

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:31.540
What're you crying for, Sachi?

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:35.000
It's embarrassing! The others might make fun of you later!

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:36.420
You're really leaving, aren't you, Bro?

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.090
Old Dohei asked me to give you this.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:43.420
Hey, I don't need all this!

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:46.930
And here. This is a parting gift from all of us.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.690
Oh, really? That's pretty cheap!

00:20:49.690 --> 00:20:50.930
Let's see...

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.530
I never asked for any of this, you know.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:04.030
You're making me take so much with me!

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.290
I have to put some in my bag so I can hold it all!

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:12.540
Look at him, putting on a brave face.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:20.170
Yabuki, the train's about to leave.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:21.720
Yeah.

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.050
All right, then! I'll be back!

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.260
Joe! Don't hurt yourself if you can help it!

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.140
Yeah. Same for you.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.680
Don't forget to write!

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:33.480
I'm not the writing type!

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:41.190
Well, uh... I can send you a postcard, at least.

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:45.190
A postcard's fine.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:46.950
Bye then.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:55.580
Later!

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:07.310
Joe!

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:07.310
<i>Bro Joe!</i>

00:22:07.310 --> 00:22:08.430
Bro!

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:12.040
Joe!

00:22:12.600 --> 00:22:13.880
Bro Joe!

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:19.400
Joe!

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:20.800
Joe! {I hear more words from sachi after Joeeee}

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:21.060
<i>Bro Joe!</i>

00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.200
Bro!

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:25.990
Joe!

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:24.400
<i>Bro!</i>

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:25.990
<i>Goodbye!{added by editor}</i>

00:22:55.440 --> 00:22:59.770
What's gonna happen to Joe now, old man?

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:01.400
Nobody knows.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:07.620
This time, Joe will decide where he's gonna go.

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:52.010
A postcard comes in from the traveling Joe.

00:24:52.010 --> 00:24:56.590
The kids set out for the seaside town Joe is in, desiring to see him.

00:24:57.270 --> 00:25:00.440
But their stomachs grow empty, night falls, and they become discouraged.

00:25:00.440 --> 00:25:02.770
Then it even starts to rain!

00:25:02.770 --> 00:25:06.570
Now, as the children go on their journey in search of Joe,

00:25:06.570 --> 00:25:07.910
which way is tomorrow!?
